{
 "what": "Decode and encode of 20000 CTAP2 authenticatorGetAssertion responses (208 bytes on average) into and out of one shared struct of views, for mbedded-cbor schema, mbedded-cbor generic and msgpack-c.",
 "why": "The earlier comparison used a timing loop of its own and showed schema encode at 21.2 against msgpack at 31.5. Its schema arm encoded from 20000 structs that owned their bytes on the heap. This run measures each arm from the same views, with Google Benchmark.",
 "how": "One binary per arm and compiler, each built twice. The eight binaries ran in turn, five rounds, each with 5 repetitions in random order. The two binaries of one arm give the noise floor. A cell is the median over 25 repetitions in million messages per second. Schema and generic do not build with clang 23, because clang has no reflection: no member named view and no member named generic in namespace cbor.",
